sequenceDiagram
    title Option B: the single-page app handles the login (Bearer token)
    participant B as Browser (SPA)
    participant A as APISIX
    participant Z as Zitadel
    participant O as OPA
    participant N as Node app

    B->>A: GET /b/ (static page, no auth)
    A->>N: forward
    N-->>B: HTML + /b/config.json
    B->>Z: redirect to /oauth/v2/authorize (code + PKCE, public client)
    Z-->>B: login page, then 302 to /b/?code=...
    B->>Z: POST /oauth/v2/token (code + PKCE verifier, CORS, no secret)
    Z-->>B: access + ID tokens, stored in sessionStorage
    B->>A: POST /api/hello (Authorization: Bearer token)
    A->>Z: JWKS (cached)
    A->>A: verify JWT signature, iss, exp
    A->>O: authz query (headers + route id)
    O->>O: server roles = data.server_roles[project][sub]
    alt writer role
        O-->>A: allow + X-Roles
        A->>N: forward + X-Roles
        N-->>B: 200
    else no writer role
        O-->>A: deny
        A-->>B: 403 writer role required
    end
